heir corresponding information. The user's information is displayed in a table, with a red button labeled \"Locked\" next to their name. The menu options on the left side of the page include \"Admin Console\", \"Dashboard\", \"Tickets\", \"Users\", \"Reports\", and \"Settings\". The \"Users\" option is currently selected, indicating that the user is viewing the list of users.\n\n**Extracted Text**\n\n* None\n\n**Errors and Warnings**\n\n* None visible\n\n**Likely Issue Category and Severity**\n\n* Category: Unknown\n* Severity: Unknown\n\n**Observed Facts vs Inference**\n\n* **Observed Facts**\n\t+ The user is signed in as A. Rao (L1 Support - Password Reset Admin).\n\t+ The user is currently on the \"Users\" page.\n\t+ The user's information is displayed in a table.\n\t+ There is a red button labeled \"Locked\" next to the user's name.\n* **Inference**\n\t+ The user may be trying to reset a password or access a restricted area.\n\t+ The \"Locked\" button may indicate that the user's account is currently locked or inactive.\n\n**Confidence Score and Notes**\n\n* CONFIDENCE SCORE: 0.8\n* CONFIDENCE LEVEL: Medium\n* CONFIDENCE REASON: The image is clear and well-lit, but the text is not particularly large or prominent, making it slightly difficult to read. Additionally, the context of the image is not entirely clear, as it appears to be a screenshot of a specific page within the CoreID Admin Console.\n\nStep 3: Caller identity verified\nNavigation: CoreID Admin Console → user profile → Identity Verification panel\nAsk the caller for at least 2 of: employee ID, manager's name, department, or last 4 digits of the phone on file. ✅ Do not send a one-time code to the user — your own admin session already satisfies the authentication requirement; this checklist is what verifies the caller is who they claim to be. If fewer than 2 items match, stop and escalate to your team lead rather than proceeding.\n\n### Visual Inspection Report (Image 3 (inline, following the text above