tion has been met. The checkbox for \"Manager name matches ticket\" is not checked, indicating that this condition has not been met. Below the options, there is a message that says \"2 of 4 confirmed - minimum required to proceed\". There is also a link to \"Settings\" at the bottom of the page.\n\n**Extracted Text**\n\nThe only text visible in the image is the title \"J. Employee - Identity Verification\" and the message \"2 of 4 confirmed - minimum required to proceed\".\n\n**Errors and Warnings**\n\nThere are no error messages or warning banners visible in the image.\n\n**Likely Issue Category and Severity**\n\nBased on the image, the likely issue category is \"Account/authentication\" with a severity of \"Medium\". This is because the page is related to verifying an employee's identity, which is a common task in account management.\n\n**Observed Facts vs Inference**\n\nOBSERVED FACTS:\n\n*   The page is titled \"J. Employee - Identity Verification\".\n*   There are two options: \"Employee ID matches ticket\" and \"Manager name matches ticket\".\n*   The checkbox for \"Employee ID matches ticket\" is checked.\n*   The checkbox for \"Manager name matches ticket\" is not checked.\n*   There is a message that says \"2 of 4 confirmed - minimum required to proceed\".\n*   There is a link to \"Settings\" at the bottom of the page.\n\nINFERENCE:\n\n*   The page is likely used to verify an employee's identity before allowing them to access certain resources or perform certain actions.\n*   The two options on the page are likely related to verifying the employee's identity through different means (e.g., employee ID and manager name).\n*   The fact that only one of the two options is checked suggests that the employee's identity has not been fully verified.\n*   The message at the bottom of the page indicates that two out of four conditions have been met, which may indicate that the employee's identity is partially verified.\n\n**Confidence Score and Notes**\n\nCONFIDENCE SCORE: 0.95\nCONFIDENCE LEVEL: High\nCONFIDENCE REASON: The image is clear and well-lit, and the text is legible. However, there is no additional context or information available to provide more insight into the issue.\n\nStep 4: Temporary password issued\nNavigation: CoreID Admin Console → user profile → Reset Password\nSelect Generate Temporary Password. Leave Force change at next sign-in checked — this is the default and it must not be disabled.\n\n### Visual Inspection Report (Image 4 (inline, following the text above)) [Confidence: 0.95 / High]:\nThe image shows a screenshot of a password reset page for an employee, with a blue button labeled \"Generate Temporary Password\" and a text box containing a temporary password. The page is titled \"Reset Password - J. Employee\" and has a white background with black text.\n\n*   **Title and Header**\n    *   The title of the page is \"Reset Password - J. Employee\".\n    *   The header of the page contains the text \"Signed in as: A. Rao (L1 Support - Password Reset Admin)\".\n*   **Temporary Password**\n    *   The temporary password is displayed in a text box.\n    *   The temporary password is \"Tq7#mVr2!IkJp9x\".\n*   **Generate Temporary Password Button**\n    *   The button is blue and labeled \"Generate Temporary Password\".\n    *   The button is located below the temporary password text box.\n*   **Background and Layout**\n    *   The background of the page is white.\n    *   The layout of the page is simple, with a clear title, header, and main content area.\n\n**Extracted Text:**\n\n*   \"Reset Password - J. Employee\"\n*   \"Signed in as: A. Rao (L1 Support - Password Reset Admin)\"\n*   \"Temporary password: Tq7#mVr2!IkJp9x\"\n*   \"Generate Temporary Password\"\n\n**Errors and Warnings:**\n\n*   None visible\n\n**Likely Issue Category and Severity:**\n\n*   Category: Account/authentication\n*   Severity: Medium\n\n**Observed Facts vs Inference:**\n\n*   **Observed Facts:**\n    *   The page is a password